<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bitterfeld</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bitterfeld is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, which grew from the late 19th century into a centre of the chemical industry, based on local brown <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-germany">East Germany</a> its chemical works made it one of the most polluted places in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Since 2007 it has been part of the town of Bitterfeld-Wolfen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bitterfeld.jpg" alt="Bitterfeld" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joeb07 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bitterfeld.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
